# Keep the host's build output OUT of the image.
#
# Without this, the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` copies the host's node_modules straight over
# the one `npm ci` just installed, which defeats the install entirely: the image ends up
# with whatever happened to be on the developer's laptop instead of what package-lock.json
# specifies. That is how adding react-markdown to package.json produced a container whose
# package.json listed it and whose node_modules did not, failing with "module not found"
# after a --no-cache rebuild.
#
# It also makes builds reproducible and much faster — node_modules is the largest thing in
# the context by far, and it was being uploaded to the daemon on every single build.
node_modules
.next
out
build

# Never bake secrets or local state into an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
*.local
